<title>GREECE: Greek finance ministry details FRN auction.</title>
<headline>Greek finance ministry details FRN auction.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's finance ministry has disclosed the following information on the auction of 125 billion drachmas ($435.3 million) of seven-year floaters.</p>
<p>    TOTAL BIDS SUBMITTED	    278.0 bln drachmas</p>
<p>    - Competitive		     232.4 bln drachmas</p>
<p>    - Non-competitive		  45.6 bln drachmas</p>
<p>Earlier, the Bank of Greece made available the following information on today's auction.</p>
<p>						 FRNs</p>
<p>    ISSUE DATE			31 July, 1997</p>
<p>    TERM					7-year</p>
<p>    FORMULA			 12-month T-Bill + 0.80%</p>
<p>    12-MONTH T-BILL			  9.60%</p>
<p>    FACE VALUE		     1.0 million drachmas</p>
<p>    MIN ACCEPTED PRICE		988,400.00</p>
<p>    AVER ACCEPTED PRICE	     990,304.25</p>
<p>    MAX OFFERED PRICE		 998,600.00</p>
<p>    AMOUNT COMPETITIVE		    125.0 bln drachmas</p>
<p>    AMOUNT NON-COMPETITIVE		 37.5 bln drachmas</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
<p>($ = 287.1 Greek Drachmas)</p>
</text>
